---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Startup Narrative Audit" description="A fixed-scope audit that turns founder conviction, customer learning and product evidence into a defensible position and 90-day test plan." pageType="service">
  <article class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="audit-inner">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Startup Narrative Audit</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Turn what your startup is learning into a position it can defend.</h1>
        <div class="prose mb-8">
          <p>You may already have strong founder conviction, useful customer conversations and meaningful product learning. But those signals do not automatically add up to a clear market position.</p>
          <p>The Startup Narrative Audit connects the evidence emerging across your company, separates what you know from what you assume and identifies the strongest argument worth testing next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="facts mb-8">
          <div><span>Format</span><strong>Fixed scope and fee</strong></div>
          <div><span>Timeline</span><strong>Two to three weeks</strong></div>
          <div><span>Best for</span><strong>B2B startups and early scaleups</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ctas"><a class="button" href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Startup%20Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry">Discuss a Startup Narrative Audit</a><a class="text-link" href="#deliverables">See what you receive ↓</a></div>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">The problem is usually upstream of the copy</h2>
        <div class="prose mb-8"><p>Founders carry the original conviction. Customers reveal how the problem is experienced. Product teams discover what changes behaviour. Sales hears the objections. Marketing is then asked to turn all of it into one confident story.</p><p>If that knowledge has not been connected, sharper wording will only disguise the gap.</p></div>
        <ul class="signal-list"><li>Your founder story works in conversation but is difficult to transfer.</li><li>Customer evidence and the public narrative do not quite match.</li><li>Product, sales and marketing explain the same problem differently.</li><li>Category ambition is moving ahead of the available proof.</li><li>You need a clear position before investing in more content or a website rewrite.</li></ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section id="deliverables" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-4">What you leave with</h2>
        <p class="intro mb-8">Six connected outputs designed to improve a decision—not produce another messaging document that sits unused.</p>
        <div class="items">
          <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Narrative diagnosis</strong>The strongest signals, contradictions and generic claims in your current position.</p></div>
          <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Evidence and assumption map</strong>What the company knows, infers, believes and still needs to learn.</p></div>
          <div><span>03</span><p><strong>Core argument</strong>A defensible central argument with supporting claims, evidence and qualifications.</p></div>
          <div><span>04</span><p><strong>Narrative gaps and risks</strong>The missing evidence and credibility risks that matter most.</p></div>
          <div><span>05</span><p><strong>Three priority opportunities</strong>Connected moves across the website, founder thinking, customer evidence or sales conversations.</p></div>
          <div><span>06</span><p><strong>90-day test plan</strong>A focused way to activate the position, capture response and decide what to revise.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">What I review</h2>
        <div class="review-grid"><div>Founder interviews and notes</div><div>Customer calls, objections and testimonials</div><div>Product and roadmap learning</div><div>Sales and customer-success insight</div><div>Website, messaging and content</div><div>Research, market signals and competitor claims</div></div>
        <p class="note">The evidence set is deliberately focused. You do not need a perfect archive, but you do need more than an untested idea.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-8">How it works</h2>
        <div class="items"><div><span>1</span><p><strong>Define the question</strong>Agree the context, audience, evidence and decision the audit must inform.</p></div><div><span>2</span><p><strong>Map the evidence</strong>Identify signals, contradictions, claims and gaps.</p></div><div><span>3</span><p><strong>Develop the position</strong>Find the strongest defensible argument and the evidence supporting it.</p></div><div><span>4</span><p><strong>Set the next test</strong>Present the findings and agree how to test the position over 90 days.</p></div></div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">A complete, focused engagement</h2>
        <div class="panel"><div class="prose"><p>I carry out the analysis and synthesis myself. The scope, inputs, deliverables, timeline and fixed fee are agreed before work begins.</p><p>The audit stands alone. Any later website, thought-leadership or editorial-system work is scoped separately.</p></div><a class="button mt-6" href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Startup%20Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry">Discuss the audit</a></div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />
      <section class="mb-8"><p class="t-label mb-6">Start with the question you cannot yet answer clearly</p><h2 class="audit-h2 mb-4">What does your company understand that its market should care about?</h2><div class="prose mb-8"><p>Tell me where the current story feels unclear, unsupported or fragmented. I will help you decide whether the audit is the right next step.</p></div><a class="button" href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Startup%20Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry">Start a conversation</a><p class="note">Not looking for a project? <a class="text-link" href="/compare-notes">Compare approaches with me instead →</a></p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .audit-inner{max-width:42rem}.prose{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.25rem}.prose p,.intro{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.8;color:var(--color-ink-secondary)}.audit-h2{font-family:var(--font-serif);font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.5vw,1.4rem);font-weight:400;color:var(--color-ink)}.facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1px;padding:1px;background:var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.facts div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.35rem;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.facts span{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.65rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-accent)}.facts strong{font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;font-weight:400;color:var(--color-ink-secondary)}.ctas{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.button{display:inline-flex;padding:.75rem 1.25rem;border-radius:3px;background:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-surface);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.05em;text-decoration:none}.button:hover{opacity:.85}.text-link{color:var(--color-accent);text-decoration:none;font-size:.875rem}.signal-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.75rem}.signal-list li{position:relative;padding-left:1.25rem;color:var(--color-ink-secondary);line-height:1.7}.signal-list li::before{content:'→';position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--color-accent)}.items{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.items>div{display:flex;gap:1.25rem;padding:1.25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.items>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}.items span{min-width:1.25rem;padding-top:.15rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.72rem;color:var(--color-accent)}.items p{margin:0;font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-ink-tertiary)}.items strong{display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem;color:var(--color-ink);font-weight:500}.review-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;padding:1px;background:var(--color-rule);border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}.review-grid div{padding:1rem 1.25rem;background:var(--color-surface-secondary);color:var(--color-ink-secondary);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.6}.note{margin-top:1.25rem;font-size:.8125rem;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-ink-tertiary)}.panel{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);border-left:2px solid var(--color-accent);border-radius:4px;background:var(--color-surface-secondary)}.mt-6{margin-top:1.5rem}@media(max-width:640px){.facts,.review-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
